{%- comment -%}
  zv-koop-fk: prints the finder_key of the package a cart line BUYS (Huren/Kopen, 2026-10-24,
  docs/koop-checkout-2026-10-24.md), 'invalid' for a malformed Koop line, or nothing.

  A Koop package line carries the line-item property Afname: Kopen (written by
  addKoopToCart() in sections/oplossingen.liquid) AND is one of the Koop products in
  pricing.config.json (packages[].koopProduct.handle, emitted by zv-pricing as
  zv_koop_fk_by_handle, 'handle:finder_key|...'). The property is the signal; the handle says
  which package, and so which installGroup. Only one of the two (the property on another
  product, or a Koop product without the property) prints 'invalid': the caller blocks checkout.

  Params (render scope can't see the section's zv_* variables, so pass them in):
    handle - item.product.handle
    afname - item.properties['Afname']
    map    - zv_koop_fk_by_handle
  Usage: capture it, then `| strip`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign kf = ''
  assign kf_pairs = map | split: '|'
  for kf_pair in kf_pairs
    assign kf_kv = kf_pair | split: ':'
    if kf_kv[0] == handle
      assign kf = kf_kv[1]
    endif
  endfor
  if afname == 'Kopen'
    if kf == ''
      echo 'invalid'
    else
      echo kf
    endif
  elsif kf != ''
    echo 'invalid'
  endif
-%}
